WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.230
About two-thirds of Indians
live in rural areas,

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.150
in villages of small family farms.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.710
About 70 per cent of rural
households depend mainly on farming.

4
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:17.070
Yet in 1991, 63.1 per cent of
India's workers were in farming.

5
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.070
By 2025, it was 41.6 per cent.

6
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.430
And many young villagers now
travel far from home to work.

7
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.350
Why do so many leave?

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.370
In this mission, you'll explore
what rural India is like:

9
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.830
its climate, its land and its jobs.

10
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.870
Then you'll map where
people move from and to,

11
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.530
and weigh what pushes them
out and pulls them in.

12
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.920
Your mission: explain why so many young
villagers in India leave for the cities.
